# realtime edge routes — paste INSIDE the central Caddy's apis.adolfrey.com
# server block (~next to the gh_webhooks handle), then `caddy reload`.
#
# Route shape (public prefix /realtime-v2 — plan §7.4; cutover = switch the
# wall's /websockets/* handles to the same blocks with a repointed prefix):
#
#   wss://apis.adolfrey.com/realtime-v2/realtime/hub → realtime:5000 /realtime/hub
#   https://apis.adolfrey.com/realtime-v2/api/*      → realtime:5000 /api/*
#
# The public surface hangs under ONE prefix and keeps the SERVICE's canonical
# paths — base URL + contract paths, verbatim (docs/CONTRACT.md). Caddy
# transparently handles the WS Upgrade; handle_path strips the prefix so the
# upstream sees its canonical routes. The operational surface (/metrics,
# /openapi, /healthz) is DENIED at the edge — scraping/contract apps use the
# internal docker door (deploy/docker-compose.yml `realtime` network).
#
# ⚠ Cloudflare Access scoping (same warning as the wall's deploy compose):
# keep the Access application for gh_webhooks LIMITED to /gh_webhooks/* — a
# host-wide Access app would 302 browser WS/negotiate calls to the Access
# login, never reaching the service's own fences.

@ops path /realtime-v2/metrics* /realtime-v2/openapi* /realtime-v2/healthz*
handle @ops {
	respond 404
}

handle_path /realtime-v2/* {
	reverse_proxy realtime:5000
}
